  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/platysilurus-mucosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Platysilurus mucosus is a predatory catfish that grows to only 20-30 cm in length. Its special features are the very long maxillary barbels and the huge caudal fin, the latter being more pronounced in juveniles than in adults.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/platysilurus-mucosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>The home of P. mucosus is the Amazon and Orinoco, where the species is widespread. The animals described here come from Peru. A second species, P. malarmo, is only found in Venezuela and Colombia and becomes remarkably larger (around 50 cm).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/platysilurus-mucosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>When catching them one must be very careful, because the pectoral fins are needle-sharp and probably also slightly poisonous. It is best to catch the animals in a comparatively very large net with as fine a mesh as possible and then scoop them out with a cup or (for larger specimens) bucket. This way you save yourself and the animals a lot of stress.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/platysilurus-mucosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>They will eat any meaty food that fits in their mouths, even smaller fish and shrimp!</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/platysilurus-mucosus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Among themselves the animals are peaceful. In community tanks you have to take care that P. mucosus get enough food, because they are, compared to other predatory catfishes, very shy.</p>"
    }
  ],
